-- title:
--   An A-generating family with independent joint residues
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring with residue field $k =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField A`, and $F$ a field extension of $L$. Let $\iota$ be a finite index type and, for each $i$, let $Fb\,i$ be a field that is a $k$-algebra, and $R\,i$ a regular prolongation of $A$ to $F$ with residue field $Fb\,i$: that is, a valuation subring $\mathcal{O}_i = (R\,i).integers$ of $F$ together with a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res}_i : \mathcal{O}_i \to Fb\,i$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_i$, such that for $x \in L$ one has $x \in A$ if and only if its image in $F$ lies in $\mathcal{O}_i$, such that $\mathrm{res}_i$ restricted to $A$ is the residue map $A \to k$ followed by $k \to Fb\,i$, and such that every nonzero $u \in F$ admits $c \in L$ with $c \cdot u \in \mathcal{O}_i$ and $\mathrm{res}_i(c \cdot u) \neq 0$. Assume the map $i \mapsto \mathcal{O}_i$ is injective; let $f \in F$ lie in every $\mathcal{O}_i$ with $\mathrm{res}_i(f)$ transcendental over $k$ for each $i$; assume $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $L(f)$ and that the fundamental equality $\sum_i [Fb\,i : k(\mathrm{res}_i(f))] = [F : L(f)]$ holds. Then for every $L$-submodule $V \subseteq F$ that is finite-dimensional over $L$, with $m = \dim_L V$, there exist $w : \mathrm{Fin}\ m \to F$ with every $w_a$ lying in $V$ and in every $\mathcal{O}_i$, such that the family $a \mapsto (i \mapsto \mathrm{res}_i(w_a))$ in $\prod_i Fb\,i$ is $k$-linearly independent, and such that every $u \in V$ lying in all the $\mathcal{O}_i$ can be written as $u = \sum_a c_a \cdot w_a$ with coefficients $c_a \in A$.
--
--   This is the explicit-basis form of constant reduction in the defectless setting of Deuring and Roquette: the $A$-module $V \cap \bigcap_i \mathcal{O}_i$ is generated by $\dim_L V$ elements whose joint residues are independent over $k$, refining the computation of $\dim_k$ of the residue span in [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.finrank_span_pi_residue_eq_finrank_of_sum_finrank_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.finrank_span_pi_residue_eq_finrank_of_sum_finrank_eq). It is applied to Riemann–Roch spaces $\mathcal{L}(N \cdot D)$ for the pole divisor of $f$, and feeds the reduction arguments for specialisations of places of modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_RegularProlongation_exists_basis_mem_integers_piResidue_linearIndependent_of_sum_finrank_eq.lean

